WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.348 --> 00:00:03.740
Bookstores are portals to amazing adventures

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.750
and stories brought right to your fingertips, literally.

3
00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.370
I'm self-educated, I taught myself from books

4
00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.190
by going to bookstores.

5
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:16.010
So I'm so passionate about reading

6
00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:17.410
because it can change your life.

7
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.270
It teaches about history, geography, humanity, poetry, love,

8
00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:26.540
just everything, everything can be found through reading.

9
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:29.160
But not everyone has access.

10
00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:32.120
I was lucky when I was younger to be able to go

11
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.320
and purchase books or go to the libraries.

12
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.627
And in Manhattan, there are 70 bookstores

13
00:00:38.627 --> 00:00:41.550
to find your next great read,

14
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.310
but head to the Bronx and there's only one.

15
00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.000
Our next guest is a Drew Gooder determined to change that

16
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.640
one book at a time.

17
00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.203
Please watch this.

18
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.150 line:15%
My name is Latanya DeVaughn and I am from the Bronx.

19
00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.670
I am the proud owner of Bronx Bound Books,

20
00:00:58.670 --> 00:00:59.970
a bookstore on wheels.

21
00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.110
Right now the Bronx only has one brick and mortar bookstore.

22
00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.090
I believe a bookstore should be a staple in every community.

23
00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.930
Sometimes the kids in the Bronx don't have access to books

24
00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.310
until they're in a school building.

25
00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.470
My mission is to make book ownership accessible

26
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.510
and affordable.

27
00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:17.523
I purchased an old bus and took out all the seats

28
00:01:17.523 --> 00:01:19.470
and flooring and converted it

29
00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.653
into a beautiful bookstore on wheels.

30
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.920
We sell books at weekly farmer's markets.

31
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.370
We visit schools, we go to shelters

32
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.100
and we also host various book drives.

33
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.860
There's such a huge misconception

34
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.810
about the people in the Bronx not wanting to read.

35
00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.500
I see young people all the time get excited about reading.

36
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.380
Some kids come on and they can't believe

37
00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:43.440
there's so many books,

38
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:46.230
others come on and just sit down and just wanna read.

39
00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.060
They think it's a genius idea

40
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.720
for a bus to be turned into a bookstore.

41
00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:53.980
Bronx Bound Books feels like more than a dream come true.

42
00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.560
It's more than I could have ever imagined it to be.

43
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.750
I wake up every day thinking of new ways to improve

44
00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.520
how to serve my community

45
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.877
and to make my dream even bigger.

46
00:02:05.145 --> 00:02:05.999
(audience cheers)
(audience applauds)

47
00:02:05.999 --> 00:02:08.916
Please welcome, Latanya DeVaughn.

48
00:02:10.151 --> 00:02:12.119
Hello.

49
00:02:12.119 --> 00:02:14.380
Where did you get this idea?

50
00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.122
I always wanted to own a bookstore.

51
00:02:17.122 --> 00:02:20.480 line:15%
All my friends knew, and I was just having a conversation.

52
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.680 line:15%
I was getting ready to quit one of my jobs,

53
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.827 line:15%
and my friend Vanessa said,

54
00:02:23.827 --> 00:02:27.020 line:15%
"You know, Latanya, you have to just do the bookstore.

55
00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.730
You keep talking about this."

56
00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:32.330
And I'm like, well, the rent is so high in the Bronx.

57
00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:33.740
Gentrification is happening

58
00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:35.720
and things are just really, really changing.

59
00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:37.700
And I said, "I'm never gonna be able to afford

60
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.600
a brick and mortar."

61
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:42.150
So one day she just showed me a picture of a book truck

62
00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.460
and that was all it took for me to find the inspiration

63
00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.870
to do a bookstore on wheels.

64
00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.964
This is so genius.
Thank you, thank you.

65
00:02:50.964 --> 00:02:54.560
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

66
00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:57.400
Now, this is personal for you.

67
00:02:57.400 --> 00:03:00.620
Will you tell us why this is personal for you?

68
00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.634
Well, I grew up with my grandmother and she was a teacher.

69
00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:07.780 line:15%
Not only did she teach the children in the Bronx,

70
00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:10.340 line:15%
sometimes on any given Saturday,

71
00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:11.640 line:15%
I could come to my living room

72
00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:13.700 line:15%
and I would see her reading to her neighbors

73
00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:14.670 line:15%
who couldn't read.

74
00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:18.600
So she would read leases, cable bills,

75
00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:20.270
and just explain to them why

76
00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:22.040
or when they needed to take their medicine.

77
00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.260
So seeing that showed me that reading was just something

78
00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.370
that could really change and save your life.

79
00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.180
I see the kids there.

80
00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.448
That's what, you know-

81
00:03:31.448 --> 00:03:34.160
(audience applauds)

82
00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.270
It does start there.

83
00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:39.720
Well, we told the publisher A Kids Company About

84
00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.740
all about you, and they're gonna give you $5,000 worth

85
00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.520
of empowering educational kids books.

86
00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:47.569
Wow.

87
00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:49.129
(audience applauds)
(audience cheers)

88
00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:52.780
And then I'm gonna match it and give you $5,000

89
00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.410
just to enable whatever you see fit

90
00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.840
and how to spend that money.
Thank you so much.

91
00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.413
Thank you so much.

92
00:04:00.625 --> 00:04:03.730
I'm so in awe of what you do

93
00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:06.730
and it is an honor to bring your story to light,

94
00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.550
to support you in our tiny, small way,

95
00:04:09.550 --> 00:04:13.210 line:15%
and just say, keep going, 'cause you are such a hero.

96
00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.043 line:15%
Thank you.

97
00:04:14.043 --> 00:04:15.340 line:15%
Thank you so much.
You are so amazing.

98
00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:16.450 line:15%
Thank you, Latanya.

99
00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.760
You can learn more about Bronx Bound Books

100
00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:22.580
on thedrewbarrymoreshow.com,

101
00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:25.188 line:15%
where you'll be featured on our website.

102
00:04:25.188 --> 00:04:28.355 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

